      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SIENNA BELLA (7) had been racing in great heart then went close again last time over 1800m at Globe Derby Park, finishing second and just a nose from the winner. Gets a soft run on the inside of the second line but may need luck at some point. Good enough to win a race of this calibre. SAL WESTER (6) form has been impressive since returning from a spell. Finished second at her latest appearance over 1609m at Port Pirie, beaten 3.5 metres, on the back of a first-up win at Port Pirie. Meets a comparable field and she can take this out. TREACHEROUS BREW (4) lines up for the first time. By Captaintreacherous and hails from the P C Bain stable. Looks to have some talent based on a recent trial win. Sure to prove tough to beat. JUST MILZY (1) broke last start and finished 7 metres from the winner in fifth over 1800m at Globe Derby Park. That followed a minor placing to kick off her career. Sure to enjoy an economical run from this draw. Worth another chance.",
